  "ownership": "Broker clones its local validated runtime path into the original factory closure. Command owns its copied environment. Helper opens one directory descriptor, creates/opens the bounded port filename relative to it, closes that directory, and retains exactly the lock descriptor until process exit. Native fixture counts descriptors before/open/close, rejects a replacement while original lock is held, then admits it only after original exit. Lock files remain stable; no unlink/reuse race. Failed setup exits before native threads and closes descriptors through original process teardown. No new task, native cleanup sponsor or long-lived allocation.",
  "bounds": "Bus 1..255; 1..7 ports each 1..255; lock filename fits 64 bytes independent of runtime path length. Tested long runtime path and full seven-port extent, missing/relative/non-directory/shared/symlink runtime rejection.",
